{"kind":"request","text":"Close the test affordance that makes personal-work storage look covered when it is not. The approved promoted-root Work-state review found that the new initialPersonalMemory prop lets the server-rendered tests supply memory directly, so the component-to-storage wiring is never exercised: four separate reversions of that wiring ship with the suite green. This is not a defect at that head, and the reviewer approved it. It is worse than an ordinary coverage gap because the rendered tests now read as though they cover the path, so the next person to touch it will believe they are protected. A stub localStorage in the harness is the reviewer's suggested fix.","body":{"conditions":"Give the UI test harness a stub globalThis.localStorage so the personal-work storage wiring is exercised rather than travelled around, then confirm the four reversions the review named now fail: not loading memory on mount, not saving it, dropping the actor from personalScope, and dropping the scope-mismatch guard. Check each one actually turns the suite red rather than assuming the stub is sufficient. Two smaller gaps from the same verdict are in scope if the stub reaches them: deleting EventTime from TopicChange ships green because the aria-label pins actor and status but not time, and WorkBoard's closed-filter branch for the non-all personal view is unexercised. Do not widen beyond the test harness and the tests themselves - no behaviour change is requested, and if you find one is needed, say so rather than making it.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}